      summary: "You tend to let the new in by default — curious across the board, drawn past the familiar.",
      body: "Your one clearly distinctive dial is openness: ideas, aesthetics, and unfamiliar experience pull on you in a way the rest of your near-typical profile has to accommodate. You tend to read past your field, question your own defaults, and find the strange interesting where others find it suspicious — the breeze through the window keeps your thinking fresh at an age when most people's has sealed shut. The costs are the window's too: what blows in is uncurated (novelty and quality are different properties), the familiar gets undervalued simply for being familiar, and steadier people around you tire of drafts.",
