      summary: "You tend to sit near typical on every dimension — and that is information, not absence.",
      body: "No dimension of your profile stands far from the population's center: your scores cluster in the broad middle where most human variation actually lives. This is not a failed result — it is a specific and somewhat uncommon one (most people show at least one strong distinctive), and it has a real signature: flexibility. Without a dominant trait steering, you can usually meet situations on their terms — sociable enough, careful enough, steady enough, open enough — where strongly-profiled people get cornered by their own settings. The corresponding cost is legibility: people struggle to summarize you, and systems built to reward distinctive edges (personal brands, niches, typologies) never quite know where to file you.",
